#: src/components/docs/api-docs-intro.tsx
msgid "Public reads need no token. Authenticated reads and writes accept standard AT Proto credentials: call your PDS with <0>atproto-proxy: {appviewDid}#{APPVIEW_SERVICE_ID}</0> (recommended), or call the AppView directly with <1>Authorization: DPoP</1> plus a DPoP proof. Token validity is checked via <2>com.atproto.server.getSession</2> on the issuer PDS; a token that cannot call <3>getSession</3> — an OAuth grant scoped only to <4>rpc:<method>?aud={appviewDid}#{APPVIEW_SERVICE_ID}</4> — is instead verified against the issuer's published keys, including its DPoP binding, and accepted for the methods that scope names."
msgstr "Public reads need no token. Authenticated reads and writes accept standard AT Proto credentials: call your PDS with <0>atproto-proxy: {appviewDid}#{APPVIEW_SERVICE_ID}</0> (recommended), or call the AppView directly with <1>Authorization: DPoP</1> plus a DPoP proof. Token validity is checked via <2>com.atproto.server.getSession</2> on the issuer PDS; a token that cannot call <3>getSession</3> — an OAuth grant scoped only to <4>rpc:<method>?aud={appviewDid}#{APPVIEW_SERVICE_ID}</4> — is instead verified against the issuer's published keys, including its DPoP binding, and accepted for the methods that scope names."

